# Track E1 NEG (SCOPE: NonDerefContainer + user equip method).
#
# `Shared[T]` is a `NonDerefContainer` per docs/language-design.md §9.2 —
# accessed via explicit `.clone()` / `.downgrade()` / etc, NEVER via deref
# to the inner. So a user equip method (`greet`) called on a `Shared[Person]`
# receiver must REJECT with `error[E_NoMethodFound]` at check-time.
#
# Pre-fix (HEAD `482f6f45`, before the terminal `MethodCall` fallthrough was
# split by DerefWrapperKind): silently accepted the call, then the C backend
# emitted a call to a nonexistent runtime symbol `Shared__Person__greet`
# → link error. The fabrication class (Core #8: known-defect ship, "both
# backends fail the same way" is not evidence of correctness).
#
# Post-fix (this track): typechecker reads `DerefWrapperKind::NonDerefContainer`
# at the terminal `MethodCall` fallthrough and emits `E_NoMethodFound` — the
# ratified diagnostic per §9.2's explicit-method-access rule.
struct Person:
    String name
    int age

equip Person:
    int greet(int e): return self.age + e

void main():
    Shared[Person] s = Shared[Person](Person("A", 30))
    print(s.greet(5))
